ass_rate":0.5873,"pass_rate_neutral":0.4524,"def_epa_per_play":-0.08168},{"week":5,"opponent":"DET","home":true,"pf":21.0,"pa":45.0,"off_snaps":70,"epa_per_play":0.02199,"pass_rate":0.7429,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6538,"def_epa_per_play":0.3262},{"week":6,"opponent":"LA","home":false,"pf":18.0,"pa":16.0,"off_snaps":70,"epa_per_play":-0.0206,"pass_rate":0.5,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5079,"def_epa_per_play":-0.1551},{"week":7,"opponent":"DEN","home":true,"pf":16.0,"pa":30.0,"off_snaps":75,"epa_per_play":-0.113,"pass_rate":0.68,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6486,"def_epa_per_play":0.2019}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2022,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.6394,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Mike LaFleur"},{"season":2024,"team":"LV","distance":0.7105,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"DAL","distance":0.7576,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Mike McCarthy"},{"season":2025,"team":"LV","distance":0.7764,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Chip Kelly"},{"season":2022,"team":"TB","distance":0.787,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"WAS","distance":0.1141,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"NO","distance":0.1188,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Brandon Staley"},{"season":2025,"team":"JAX","distance":0.2826,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Anthony Campanile"},{"season":2024,"team":"CHI","distance":0.2909,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"BUF","distance":0.329,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Cardinals are 2-5 through week 7 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 208 to 142. The offense has been carrying the team, ranking 19th in EPA per play while the defense sits 27th in EPA allowed. What sets them apart is the 3rd fewest backs in the backfield in the league.","offense":"The Cardinals offense has been a little below average by EPA per play so far. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 3rd fewest backs in the backfield and the 2nd lowest RPO rate in the league. Jacoby Brissett has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Trey McBride, who has drawn 29% of the targets.","defense":"The Cardinals have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 27th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per rush, where it ranks 10th, and its weakest has been explosive play rate allowed, where it ranks 31st. Josh Sweat has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Budda Baker, who has 3.5 sacks, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 8th lowest in the league.","special":"The Cardinals have been one of the most conservative teams on fourth down, going for it on only 8% of their short-yardage chances. Their kickers have made 89% of field goals, which is a little above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into tight ends, about 10% of the money on the books.","players":"Jacoby Brissett has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,600 yards. Trey McBride has been the clear top target with 29% of the looks and 472 receiving yards. The backfield has been a committee led by Jeremiyah Love and Tyler Allgeier. On defense, Budda Baker leads the team with 3.5 sacks.","coaching":"Mike LaFleur is calling the offense as head coach and Nick Rallis is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2022 Jets under Mike LaFleur and the 2024 Raiders. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Commanders and the 2025 Saints under Brandon Staley.","trends":"The offense went from 23rd in EPA per play in 2025 to 19th so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 27th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 27th so far this season, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was pre-snap motion rate, which went from 44% to 62%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}